<title>EGYPT: Egypt buys 400,000 tonnes French wheat.</title>
<headline>Egypt buys 400,000 tonnes French wheat.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Egyptian state's main grain buyer said on Sunday he was buying 400,000 tonnes of French soft red wheat -- 100,000 tonnes at $167 FOB for loading in October and 300,000 tonnes at $163.90 FOB for loading in November.</p>
<p>The state's General Authority for Supply Commodities had also asked for bids for U.S. wheat but the vice chairman of the authority, Samir Shakankiri, said it did not buy any. &quot;America is out of the competition,&quot; he told Reuters.</p>
</text>
